  "content": {
    "id": "p36-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "A tennis team has a probability of 76% of winning a match when they are at home and 45% of winning a match when they are away. If the team plays 58% of their matches away, find the probability that the team:\n\nGive answers to the nearest whole percent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p36-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "wins their match given that they are away",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$45\\%$",
          "worked": "$$P(\\text{win}\\mid\\text{away})=0.45=45\\%.$$ This probability is given.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "are at home given that they win a match",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$55\\%$",
          "worked": "A tree diagram is useful here. Split first into home and away, then into win and lose.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{home})&=1-0.58=0.42\\\\P(\\text{home}\\cap\\text{win})&=0.42\\times0.76=0.3192\\\\P(\\text{away}\\cap\\text{win})&=0.58\\times0.45=0.261\\\\P(\\text{win})&=0.3192+0.261=0.5802\\\\P(\\text{home}\\mid\\text{win})&=\\frac{P(\\text{home}\\cap\\text{win})}{P(\\text{win})}\\\\P(\\text{home}\\mid\\text{win})&=\\frac{0.3192}{0.5802}\\\\P(\\text{home}\\mid\\text{win})&\\approx55\\%\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "are away given that they lose a match.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$76\\%$",
          "worked": "Use the lose branches of the home/away tree.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{lose}\\mid\\text{away})&=1-0.45=0.55\\\\P(\\text{lose}\\mid\\text{home})&=1-0.76=0.24\\\\P(\\text{away}\\cap\\text{lose})&=0.58\\times0.55=0.319\\\\P(\\text{home}\\cap\\text{lose})&=0.42\\times0.24=0.1008\\\\P(\\text{lose})&=0.319+0.1008=0.4198\\\\P(\\text{away}\\mid\\text{lose})&=\\frac{P(\\text{away}\\cap\\text{lose})}{P(\\text{lose})}\\\\P(\\text{away}\\mid\\text{lose})&=\\frac{0.319}{0.4198}\\\\P(\\text{away}\\mid\\text{lose})&\\approx76\\%\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      }
    ]
  },
